---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '~/components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Mindful handles information when you visit the site: no analytics, third-party hosting and images, and plain-language detail."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[52rem]">
    <PageHeader title="How we treat your visit." crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Mindful is a small, read-only website of essays. We do <strong>not</strong> run Google
        Analytics, advertising trackers, or similar analytics products. We are not in the business
        of profiling readers.
      </p>

      <h2>What you share by simply browsing</h2>
      <p>
        When you open a page, technical information travels the way it always does on the web: your
        browser asks servers for files, and those servers see data such as your IP address, the page
        or file requested, and rough timing. That is normal internet plumbing, not something unique
        to Mindful.
      </p>

      <h2>Who helps us deliver the site</h2>
      <p>We rely on a few services so the site loads quickly and stays online:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> sits in front of our domain for DNS and network services (for
          example routing, security, and performance). Cloudflare processes visitor traffic as part
          of that role. Their own policies describe what they collect and why.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Railway</strong> hosts the built site. When you request a page or file, Railway
          (and any caching or edge network they use to deliver static files) may process the same
          kind of technical data as any host.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Placeholder images</strong> on some essays come from <strong>Picsum</strong> (and
          its CDN). Your browser loads those images directly from their infrastructure, which means
          Picsum or its providers may see technical data tied to that request, the same way any
          external image host would.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>
        We bundle our web fonts with the site (via Fontsource packages built into our CSS). We do
        <strong>not</strong> load fonts from Google Fonts or another remote font service in the page
        head, so visiting Mindful does not send a separate font request to Google for typography.
      </p>

      <h2>Offline support (service worker)</h2>
      <p>
        Mindful registers a small <strong>service worker</strong> so pages and same-origin assets
        can be cached on <em>your device</em> for speed and a simple offline fallback. That cache
        stays on your device; it is not a copy we read on our servers.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and similar storage</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use cookies for marketing or analytics. Any storage tied to the service worker is
        for technical caching as described above, not for cross-site tracking.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Mindful is written for adults reflecting on wellbeing. It is not aimed at collecting data
        from children. If you are a parent or guardian with a concern, please use contact options we
        publish elsewhere when available.
      </p>

      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <p>
        If our stack or practices change in a way that matters for privacy, we will update this page
        and note the spirit of the change here. This is a transparency page, not a contract; for
        rules about using the site, see <a href="/terms">Terms of use</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
